---
title: Pitta Bread
yield: 8%pittas
course: Bread
cuisine: Greek
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
---

Mix the @fast-acting dried yeast{7%g}(1 sachet) with the @warm water{300%ml} in a large bowl. Leave to sit for ~{5%minutes} until the yeast is bubbly.

Add the @plain flour{500%g}, @salt{2%tsp}, and @olive oil{1%tbsp}, to the yeast mixture. Bring the mixture together into a rough soft dough. Tip onto a lightly floured work surface. Knead for 5 to ~{10%minutes} until it is soft, smooth, and elastic. Use the minimum extra flour to prevent the dough from sticking to keep the pittas light and airy. Place in a lightly oiled bowl, cover with a tea towel, and leave to double in size for ~{1%hour}.

Place a #pizza stone{} (or large baking tray) in the middle of the oven and preheat to 230°C.

Divide the dough into eight balls, and flatten each into a disc with the palm of your hand. On a lightly floured surface, roll each disc into a 15×20cm oval 3-5mm thick.

Cook the pittas directly on the pizza stone for 4 to ~{5%minutes}, or until puffed up and a pale golden colour. Wrap each hot pitta in a clean tea towel once it's baked to keep it soft while the others cook.